From: Philip Balister <philip@balister.org>
Subject: [PATCH] qa_SchedulerLifecycle: build without the cross-object library cases

The GR_TEST_WITH_BLOCK_LIBRARY cases load the cross_object_library fixture
from TESTS_BINARY_PATH, the build-host ${B}/core/test path compiled into the
binary. That path does not exist once the test is installed on the target
for ptest, and it trips the buildpaths QA check. Drop the define so the rest
of the test still builds and runs; upstream already builds it this way when
block plugins are disabled.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific ptest packaging]

Signed-off-by: Philip Balister <philip@balister.org>
---
--- a/core/test/CMakeLists.txt	2026-10-13 16:11:30.665023010 -0400
+++ b/core/test/CMakeLists.txt	2026-10-13 16:11:30.673269420 -0400
@@ -205,7 +205,6 @@
 
   # the cases with blocks or a scheduler from a shared object load that object
   add_dependencies(qa_SchedulerLifecycle cross_object_library)
-  target_compile_definitions(qa_SchedulerLifecycle PRIVATE GR_TEST_WITH_BLOCK_LIBRARY)
 
   # the cases compare the values that a shared object's code reads with the program's
   add_ut_test(qa_SharedObjectState)
